<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Alexander, Margrave of Brandenburg-Ansbach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1736–1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Alexander was the last Margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-ansbach">Brandenburg-Ansbach</a>, from 1757, who also inherited Brandenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a> in 1769. Like his predecessors he hired out soldiers to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> during the American war. In 1791 he gave up both principalities to his Prussian cousins in return for a pension and retired to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-alexander-margrave-of-brandenburg-ansbach.jpg" alt="Charles Alexander, Margrave of Brandenburg-Ansbach" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Gotthard Naumann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gotthard_Naumann_-_Markgraf_Karl_Alexander_-_Bayerische_Staatsgem%C3%A4ldesammlungen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
